+/**
+ * Abstract base class for every threaded, cancelable install "step" in PIM
+ * (e.g. pimCopyLoop, pimMSILoop, pimSFXLoop, pimScriptLoop, pimShortcutLoop,
+ * pimRegEditLoop, pimServiceLoop, pimPsfLoop, pimDownloadLoop) and for
+ * pimEntitlement itself, which also derives from pimLoop so an entire
+ * product install/uninstall runs as one cancelable, pausable unit.
+ *
+ * Responsibilities:
+ * - Own the threaded execution contract (Execute/Cancel/Pause/Resume/Wait/Kill).
+ * - Own progress/completion state (mCancel/mDone/mPause/mInProgress) behind Mutex.
+ * - Accumulate newline-joined error/warning text reported by subclasses.
+ * - Hold the pimXmlFile this Loop instance operates against (xmlPtr), without
+ *   owning it.
+ *
+ * Dependencies:
+ * - thrThread (base class, external btk toolkit) supplies the OS thread mechanics.
+ * - thrMutex / thrSemaphore (external btk) guard shared state and back Pause/Resume.
+ * - pimXmlFile, whose own PreRead/PreWrite locking protects the underlying DOM
+ *   document across the multiple Loop threads that may share one entitlement's XML.
+ *
+ * Thread safety: mCancel/mDone/mPause/mInProgress and the Errors/Warnings buffers
+ * are read/written only under Mutex (recursive). Subclasses are responsible for
+ * polling IsCancelFlagSet()/IsPaused() from their own OnExecute() loop body.
+ */
 class pimLoop : public thrThread
 {
